    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking at a contract for some electronic components moving from south korea to germany. It says CIF. can u explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under Incoterms 2020, CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) means that the seller is responsible for the costs associated with transporting the goods from their place of shipment in South Korea to the buyer's destination in Germany. This includes the cost of the goods themselves, insurance coverage for the goods during this time, and freight (transportation) costs. However, the seller does not bear the risk of damage during transportation until it is transferred to the buyer's risk upon delivery.",
      "source": "target",
